# Video bytes are NOT committed. The stills in ../assets are 80 MB; a full
# NOAA video harvest is ~9 GB, which does not belong in git history.
#
# Nothing is lost: every clip in ../video_rights.json carries its direct_url
# and the sha256 of the exact bytes, so `imagery_video.py --harvest` refetches
# them and `--verify` proves the refetch is byte-identical to what was
# rights-checked. The manifest is the artefact; these files are a cache.
*
!.gitignore
